# FetchCatch workspace guardrails

When editing files under `.fetchcatch/`:

## Never do

- Change `id` GUIDs on flows or response types already synced to the server
- Invent or guess `apiSourceId` values — they must exist in the tenant
- Set `"publish": true` unless the user explicitly asks to publish
- Edit `sync-state.json` by hand
- Edit or delete `*.remote.json` conflict snapshots
- Touch `~/.fetchcatch/` credentials

## Always do

- Use node ids matching `^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$`
- Keep `schemaVersion: 1` unless docs manifest specifies otherwise
- Wire condition edges with `"when": "true"` and `"when": "false"`
- Add `description` on new nodes
- After edits, recommend `fcc plan` before `fcc apply`
- On conflicts, use `fcc diff` and `fcc resolve` — never force-overwrite blindly

## Sync workflow

```bash
fcc plan --json    # preview changes
fcc apply --dry-run
fcc apply          # only after user confirms
```

Read `.fetchcatch/AGENTS.md` and https://fetchcatch.com/docs/v0.1/ai-agent-guide.md before large changes.
